-- by hand: change the template or the generator and regenerate.
-- Lindenmoor seam regrade in Ye (owner 2026-10-24: "Could you rebuild the ground height along the seam in studio with
-- all of the assets you currently have?"; Ruling 21 done in place). Run in Studio EDIT, Ye only, never in Play:
--   python -I Art/Tools/rbxc.py luau "placeId: 106992859583940" Edit @regrade_seam.lua
-- MODE:
--   "apply": refuses if already applied (attribute LindenmoorSeamRegrade on World.Map.LindenmoorExpansion) or if the
--            backup RenseiBackups["Pre-SeamRegrade_2026-10-24"] exists, or if any part it replaces is not exactly where
--            the plan says. Then, in a pcall that undoes everything on an error, and recorded with ChangeHistoryService
--            when Studio allows it:
--              * builds the new stepped ground (Top slabs and Side blocks cloned from the parts they replace, so
--                Material, Color, MaterialVariant and tags match; RenseiNoGrip set exactly on crag pieces) in the same
--                Ground_<i>_<j> tile models, marked with the attribute LindenmoorSeamNew;
--              * covers Ye's edge cells whose own top is below the Baseplate's (the bare-Baseplate points) with 1-stud
--                slabs cloned from the Ye part there, in LindenmoorExpansion.SeamRegradeFill (Ye's parts untouched);
--              * moves every replaced part into the backup: tags stripped and kept as JSON in RegionKitTags, its old
--                path in LindenmoorSeamPath, an ObjectValue LindenmoorSeamParent to its parent;
--              * moves every expansion object standing on a changed cell by that cell's height change (route pieces
--                are re-tilted between their two ends so the route stays continuous), its old CFrame in
--                LindenmoorSeamFrom (and old Size in LindenmoorSeamSize for a re-tilted piece);
--            then runs the checks below.
--   "undo":  destroys the new parts, puts every backed-up part back with its tags, returns every moved object, deletes
--            the backup and clears the attribute. Refuses if nothing is applied, and while a later fix built on the
--            regrade is applied: the road cut (LindenmoorRoadCut), the seam pits (LindenmoorSeamPits) or the gorge fix
--            (LindenmoorGorgeFix, final review I2). Undo those first.
--   "check": the checks only: the boundary jumps (Ye's top vs the expansion's, every Ye<->expansion boundary pair, by
--            class), the bare-Baseplate scan (4-stud grid over the whole map), moved objects' bases against the
--            ground under them, the part count, and steps along every route's centreline.
--   "test":  snapshot, apply, checks, undo, snapshot; reports whether the two snapshots are equal.
--@@MODE@@
--@@OLD@@
--@@NEW@@
--@@DELTA@@
--@@PAIRS@@
--@@FILL@@
